
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:listnick@

%9Description:%9

    Lists the kept nicks: "Keeping <nick> in [network] (active)", or
    "(inactive)" when keeping is paused after a manual nick change, or
    "(refused: ...)" for a nick that cannot be kept (not one IRC word, or
    longer than the server's NICKLEN). A nick kept by keepnick_auto for
    one connection says "this connection" as well. An empty list prints
    "No nicks in keep list".

%9Examples:%9

    /LISTNICK

%9See also:%9 KEEPNICK, UNKEEPNICK

